message: "If you use, reference, reproduce, or build upon this work, please cite it using the metadata below."

title: "Fujitsu D3313-E1 BIOS Recovery and Firmware Analysis"

authors:
  - family-names: "Bencze"
    given-names: "Péter"
    email: "bencze.peter86@proton.me"

abstract: >-
  A forensic-style technical investigation of BIOS recovery, SPI firmware
  acquisition, machine-specific OEM data, Realtek network-controller identity,
  eFuse state, and selective firmware restoration on a Fujitsu FUTRO S930
  equipped with a Fujitsu D3313-E1 mainboard. The investigation documents
  duplicate cryptographically verified SPI acquisitions, comparison with
  official Fujitsu R1.16 firmware, identification of a 64 KiB machine-specific
  OEM/manufacturing region, analysis of post-recovery loss of permanent LAN
  identity, direct Realtek EEPROM/eFuse diagnostics, internal SPI acquisition
  under Linux, and restoration of the original platform identity by selectively
  rewriting only the demonstrated OEM region.

